{- | The compiler's single-stage probe gates, as one runner over a table of
   rows.

   Six shell gates used to do this, one script per probe, each a near-copy of
   the same loop: spawn `test/bin/<entry>_main` over a corpus of `.mdk`
   files, strip the native runtime's trailing `()`, and diff the result
   against a committed golden sitting beside each fixture. The probe, the
   corpus and the golden's suffix are the data; the loop is not. The rows
   here name them:

   | retired gate | probe | corpus | golden |
   |---|---|---|---|
   | `diff_compiler_diagnostics` | `diagnostics_main` | `resolve`/`exhaust`/`check_match` fixtures | `.analyze.golden` |
   | `diff_compiler_exhaust` | `exhaust_main` | `test/exhaust_fixtures` | `.expected` |
   | `diff_compiler_fmt` | `fmt_main` | `test/fmt_fixtures` + `test/parse_fixtures` | `.fmt.golden` |
   | `diff_compiler_lex_files` | `lex_main` | the lexer and twelve stdlib modules | `.lextok.golden` |
   | `diff_compiler_lint` | `lint_main` | `test/lint_fixtures` | `.expected` |
   | `diff_compiler_lint_fix` | `lint_fix_main` | `test/lint_fix_fixtures` | `.fixed` |

   `diff_compiler_lex_files`' corpus is REAL SOURCE, not fixtures: the
   lexer's own 2,775 lines plus twelve stdlib modules, which exercise
   whatever real code actually uses (block comments, the full operator set)
   rather than what a curated corpus remembered to include.

   `diff_compiler_lint`'s probe reads an environment variable the other five
   do not: `lint_main` builds its stdlib index from `$MEDAKA_ROOT/stdlib`, and
   indexes NOTHING when that is unset, which silences every
   `rule-stdlib-reimpl` finding. Eight of its 46 fixtures answer differently
   without it and the goldens are the with-index answer, so an unset
   `MEDAKA_ROOT` reds those eight rather than passing on an empty index.
   `medaka gate run` sets it for every gate (`gate_cmd.gateArgs`); a bare
   `medaka test --native` on this file inherits whatever the shell had.

   Eight more retired scripts do NOT fit `Row` — each spawns its probe more
   than once per fixture, with per-fixture routing, injected environment
   variables, stdin, or a comparison that is not a text diff, which one
   (probe, corpus, goldenSuffix) triple can't express. Each keeps its own
   block below instead, over the SAME two predicates as a `Row`: a spawn's
   exit code and stderr, and its stdout against a golden.

   - `diff_compiler_draft_semantic` grades FIVE spawns per fixture (a
     baseline plus four `MEDAKA_DRAFT_MUTATION`-controlled runs), only the
     first of which is diffed against a golden.
   - `diff_compiler_references_correctness` dumps a whole 1-4-module
     project per fixture via `refindex_main --dump`, not a per-file corpus
     loop, over eight fixture directories.
   - `diff_compiler_effect_hole` / `diff_compiler_effect_param` spawn BOTH
     the native CLI (`./medaka check`) and `test/bin/check_main` over
     inline-heredoc fixtures, asserting on type-scheme substrings and
     rejection diagnostics rather than a single stdout diff.
   - `diff_compiler_typecheck_errors` routes each fixture to one or both of
     two drivers (`typecheck_main`, `check_main`) by a per-fixture
     "prelude-dependent" list — not expressible as one row's single probe.
   - `diff_compiler_repl` feeds a whole session transcript to its probe over
     STDIN, which no `Row` has a path for.
   - `diff_compiler_analyze_project` compares two whole-project diagnostic
     dumps SEMANTICALLY: per file, the MULTISET of `(severity, message)`
     pairs and the START position of each located diagnostic, against a
     frozen `oracle.json` that has no regenerator. Ordering is not part of
     the claim, so a text diff would report a reordering as a failure.
   - `diff_compiler_test` grades its corpus against per-module goldens AND
     an eleven-case battery over the same probe — exit codes, two whole
     pinned reports, and substrings that must and must not appear — which
     one row's single stdout diff cannot express.

   Two of the sixteen retired scripts are not corpus-and-golden shaped and
   are not bent into rows either — the two tests at the foot of this file:

   - `diff_compiler_new` scaffolded ONE project tree and compared the whole
     TREE (file list and bytes) against `test/new_golden/myapp`. There is no
     corpus and no per-fixture golden, and `test/capture_goldens.sh new` is a
     stale no-op, so a mismatch is reviewed and hand-copied rather than
     captured.
   - `diff_compiler_entry_exit_codes` pins #440: five error paths through the
     emitter probe's `driveModules`, each asserted on the exit code AND on
     stdout staying empty AND on stderr carrying a diagnostic, plus a control
     proving those five discriminate. Its inputs are synthesized, three of
     them being a file that must NOT exist, which no corpus can hold.

   The registry entry keeps `diff_compiler_fmt`'s name so the merged gate
   inherits that gate's measured cost history rather than arriving uncosted
   (`gate_cost.baselineKey` reads the `run` path, and `medaka gate balance`
   hard-refuses on a gate with no cost sample). Each retired gate's own
   baseline row is dropped in the commit that retires it, so the baseline
   holds no row the registry cannot key — `test/gate_cost_ingest.sh`'s
   `--registry` pass would drop it anyway, a release later. A failure names
   the RETIRED gate it belongs to, so the shared registry name never hides
   which property broke.

   Every row also grades what the scripts did not: the probe's exit code and
   its stderr, not stdout alone (`probe_runner.processFailure`). Runs under
   `medaka test --native`.

   Every block below also writes down how many units it grades, checked by
   `probe_runner.countFloor` — the non-row half of what `Row.fixtures` does.
   A corpus that grew reds until the number beside it is updated to match,
   which is the price of a corpus that shrinks reding too. -}

import compiler_cli_test_support.{chompNewlines, stripUnitAutoPrint}
import fs.{fixtureDirs, fixtureFiles}
import io.{runVerb}
import json.{Json, asArray, asInt, asString, get, parse}
import list.{dropWhile, lookup, partitionResults, somes, sort, span}
import path.{basename, dirname, stem}
import probe_runner.{
  Row, countFloor, diffNote, errorPathFailures, gradeProbeRows, processFailure,
  report, scaffoldFailures, stderrTail
}
import string.{
  contains, endsWith, join, lines, replaceAll, split, startsWith, stripPrefix,
  toInt, toLower, trim, unlines
}
import test_process.{
  boundedVerb, boundedVerbSeconds, medakaRoot, scratchDir, underRoot
}

-- | The stdlib modules `diff_compiler_lex_files` lexed, in its own order.
lexCorpus : List String
lexCorpus = [
  "compiler/frontend/lexer.mdk",
  "stdlib/core.mdk",
  "stdlib/list.mdk",
  "stdlib/array.mdk",
  "stdlib/string.mdk",
  "stdlib/map.mdk",
  "stdlib/set.mdk",
  "stdlib/io.mdk",
  "stdlib/hash_map.mdk",
  "stdlib/hash_set.mdk",
  "stdlib/vector.mdk",
  "stdlib/json.mdk",
  "stdlib/test.mdk",
]

rows : List Row
rows = [
  Row {
    gate = "diff_compiler_diagnostics",
    probe = "test/bin/diagnostics_main",
    corpus = [
      "test/resolve_fixtures", "test/exhaust_fixtures",
      "test/check_match_fixtures"
    ],
    prelude = ["stdlib/runtime.mdk", "stdlib/core.mdk"],
    goldenSuffix = ".analyze.golden",
    sorted = True,
    stripUnit = True,
    fixtures = 42,
  },
  Row {
    gate = "diff_compiler_exhaust",
    probe = "test/bin/exhaust_main",
    corpus = ["test/exhaust_fixtures"],
    prelude = [],
    goldenSuffix = ".expected",
    sorted = True,
    stripUnit = True,
    fixtures = 6,
  },
  Row {
    gate = "diff_compiler_fmt",
    probe = "test/bin/fmt_main",
    corpus = ["test/fmt_fixtures", "test/parse_fixtures"],
    prelude = [],
    goldenSuffix = ".fmt.golden",
    sorted = False,
    stripUnit = True,
    fixtures = 87,
  },
  Row {
    gate = "diff_compiler_lex_files",
    probe = "test/bin/lex_main",
    corpus = lexCorpus,
    prelude = [],
    goldenSuffix = ".lextok.golden",
    sorted = False,
    stripUnit = True,
    fixtures = 13,
  },
  Row {
    gate = "diff_compiler_lint",
    probe = "test/bin/lint_main",
    corpus = ["test/lint_fixtures"],
    prelude = [],
    goldenSuffix = ".expected",
    sorted = True,
    stripUnit = True,
    fixtures = 46,
  },
  Row {
    gate = "diff_compiler_lint_fix",
    probe = "test/bin/lint_fix_main",
    corpus = ["test/lint_fix_fixtures"],
    prelude = [],
    goldenSuffix = ".fixed",
    sorted = False,
    stripUnit = False,
    fixtures = 23,
  },
]

test "every probe reproduces its corpus's goldens" = gradeProbeRows rows

test "`medaka new`'s scaffold matches its golden tree" =
  report
    "scaffold"
    (scaffoldFailures "test/bin/new_main" "myapp" "test/new_golden/myapp" 4)

test "entry-probe error paths exit nonzero with an empty artifact" =
  report "error-path" (errorPathFailures "test/bin/llvm_emit_modules_main" 6)

-- # Shared helpers for the rows below that do not fit `Row`

{- | Runs `cmd` with `name=value` set in its environment, on top of
   `boundedVerb`'s own `env`-then-`perl` wrapping (`test_process.mdk`): a
   bare `env` first argument is itself a valid command name, so `env` sees
   it, re-execs `env name=value cmd args...`, and the variable reaches
   `cmd`. -}
withEnv : String ->
  String ->
  String ->
  List String ->
  <Exec> Result String (Int, String, String)
withEnv name value cmd args =
  boundedVerb "env" (["\{name}=\{value}", cmd] ++ args)

-- | `text` contains every string in `needles`.
containsAll : String -> List String -> Bool
containsAll text needles = all (n => contains n text) needles

-- | `text` reads as a rejected `check` run: a parse/type-error vocabulary
-- word, case-insensitively.
hasParseErr : String -> Bool
hasParseErr text =
  let low = toLower text
  contains "parse error" low
    || contains "type error" low
    || contains "unbound" low
    || contains "unknown" low

{- | The `# TYPES_USER` section of a snapshot `.md`'s lines: everything
   after a line reading exactly `# TYPES_USER`, up to the next `# `-headed
   line or the end. -}
typesUserSection : List String -> List String
typesUserSection ls = takeSection (dropWhile (/= "# TYPES_USER") ls)

takeSection : List String -> List String
takeSection [] = []
takeSection (_ :: rest) = takeUntilHeader rest

takeUntilHeader : List String -> List String
takeUntilHeader [] = []
takeUntilHeader (l :: rest)
  | startsWith "# " l = []
  | otherwise = l :: takeUntilHeader rest

-- | The lines of `want` absent, verbatim, from `got`.
missingLines : List String -> List String -> List String
missingLines want got = filter (l => not (elem l got)) want

{- | Every committed `# TYPES_USER` line of the snapshot at `snapshotRel`
   appears verbatim in `host`'s own TYPES output over `fix` — the
   subset-membership check `diff_compiler_effect_hole`/`_effect_param`
   shared (#81 Stage C2: the prelude scheme table is pinned once elsewhere,
   so only the user schemes are re-checked here). -}
effectTypesSuperset : String ->
  String ->
  String ->
  String ->
  String ->
  <Exec, FileRead, IO> Option String
effectTypesSuperset snapshotRel host rt core fix =
  let snap = underRoot snapshotRel
  match readFile snap
    Err e => Some "missing snapshot \{snap}: \{e}"
    Ok snapRaw =>
      let want = typesUserSection (lines (chompNewlines snapRaw))
      match boundedVerb host [rt, core, fix]
        Err e => Some "native-host TYPES: could not spawn check_main: \{e}"
        Ok (code, out, err) =>
          match processFailure "check_main" "native-host TYPES" code err
            Some m => Some m
            None =>
              let got = lines (chompNewlines (stripUnitAutoPrint out))
              let missing = missingLines want got
              if missing == [] then
                None
              else
                let body = unlines (map (l => "  missing: \{l}") missing)
                Some "native-host TYPES missing # TYPES_USER lines:\n\{body}"

-- # `diff_compiler_draft_semantic`

draftSemanticFixturesDir : String
draftSemanticFixturesDir = "test/draft_semantic_fixtures"

{- | The one `main_*.mdk` entry directly under `dir`, or an error naming how
   many were found — the fixture is malformed unless there is exactly
   one. -}
draftSemanticEntry : String -> <FileRead> Result String String
draftSemanticEntry dir = match fixtureFiles dir
  Err e => Err "\{dir}: \{e}"
  Ok paths =>
    match (filter
      (p => startsWith "main_" (basename p) && endsWith ".mdk" p)
      paths)
      [e] => Ok e
      es =>
        Err
          "\{dir}: expected exactly one main_*.mdk entry, found \{intToString (length es)}"

{- | Runs the probe under `mutation` (unmutated when `""`) and asserts
   `wantReceipt` appears in its output, plus `wantDiffCount` when given —
   the shared shape of every `MEDAKA_DRAFT_MUTATION` check the retired
   script ran. `wantDiffCount` is `None` for the positive control, whose
   difference count is asserted NONZERO by its own caller instead of a
   fixed string here. -}
draftSemanticAssert : String ->
  String ->
  String ->
  Option String ->
  String ->
  String ->
  String ->
  String ->
  <Exec, IO> Result String String
draftSemanticAssert label mutation wantReceipt wantDiffCount bin rt core entry =
  let spawn =
    if mutation == "" then
      boundedVerb bin [rt, core, entry]
    else
      withEnv "MEDAKA_DRAFT_MUTATION" mutation bin [rt, core, entry]
  match spawn
    Err e => Err "\{label}: could not spawn: \{e}"
    Ok (code, out, _) =>
      if code /= 0 then
        Err
          "\{label}: exited \{intToString code} instead of producing a receipt"
      else
        let text = chompNewlines out
        if not (contains wantReceipt text) then
          Err "\{label}: expected receipt not found: \{wantReceipt}"
        else match wantDiffCount
          Some needle =>
            if contains needle text then
              Ok text
            else
              Err
                "\{label}: expected difference-count summary not found: \{needle}"
          None => Ok text

methodIfaceReceipt : String
methodIfaceReceipt =
  "(receipt method-iface methodIfaceTable elaborated-graph DIFFERENT)"

{- | Everything wrong with one `draft_semantic_fixtures/<name>/` fixture:
   the baseline draft (diffed against its golden), and the four mutation
   controls that prove the golden's comparator can actually observe a
   copied-field mismatch rather than only ever printing MATCH. -}
draftSemanticFixtureFailure : String -> <Exec, FileRead, IO> Option String
draftSemanticFixtureFailure dir = match draftSemanticEntry dir
  Err e => Some e
  Ok entry =>
    let name = basename dir
    let bin = underRoot "test/bin/draft_semantic_main"
    let rt = underRoot "stdlib/runtime.mdk"
    let core = underRoot "stdlib/core.mdk"
    match boundedVerb bin [rt, core, entry, dir]
      Err e => Some "\{name}: could not spawn draft_semantic_main: \{e}"
      Ok (code, out, err) => match processFailure (basename bin) name code err
        Some m => Some m
        None =>
          let baseline = chompNewlines out
          if not (contains "(different 0)" baseline) then
            Some
              "\{name}: baseline draft has a transport mismatch (or no summary)"
          else
            draftSemanticChecks name bin rt core entry dir baseline

draftSemanticChecks : String ->
  String ->
  String ->
  String ->
  String ->
  String ->
  String ->
  <Exec, FileRead, IO> Option String
draftSemanticChecks name bin rt core entry dir baseline =
  let malformed =
    draftSemanticAssert
      "\{name}: malformed-field control"
      "method-iface"
      methodIfaceReceipt
      (Some "(different 1)")
      bin
      rt
      core
      entry
  match malformed
    Err e => Some e
    Ok _ =>
      let provenance =
        draftSemanticAssert
          "\{name}: provenance control"
          "method-iface-provenance"
          methodIfaceReceipt
          (Some "(different 1)")
          bin
          rt
          core
          entry
      match provenance
        Err e => Some e
        Ok _ =>
          let control =
            draftSemanticAssert
              "\{name}: unrelated positive control"
              "unrelated-control"
              "(receipt module-emitter-projection elaborateModules elaborated-modules DIFFERENT)"
              None
              bin
              rt
              core
              entry
          match control
            Err e => Some e
            Ok text =>
              if contains "(different 0)" text then
                Some
                  "\{name}: unrelated positive control could not observe its unrelated module"
              else
                draftSemanticIsolation name bin rt core entry dir baseline

draftSemanticIsolation : String ->
  String ->
  String ->
  String ->
  String ->
  String ->
  String ->
  <Exec, FileRead, IO> Option String
draftSemanticIsolation name bin rt core entry dir baseline =
  match withEnv "MEDAKA_DRAFT_MUTATION" "same-process" bin [rt, core, entry]
    Err e => Some "\{name}: P -> P+U -> P control could not spawn: \{e}"
    Ok (code, out, _) =>
      if code /= 0 then
        Some "\{name}: P -> P+U -> P control exited \{intToString code}"
      else if chompNewlines out /= baseline then
        Some
          "\{name}: P changed after constructing unrelated P+U in the same process"
      else match readFile "\{dir}/draft.golden"
        Err e => Some "\{name}: no readable golden: \{e}"
        Ok raw =>
          let want = chompNewlines raw
          if want == baseline then
            None
          else
            Some "\{name}: \{diffNote want baseline}"

-- # `diff_compiler_references_correctness`

-- | The eight project fixtures the retired script dumped, in its own
-- order. `test/references_fixtures/query` is a DIFFERENT gate's corpus
-- (JSONL query goldens, not `expected.golden`) and stays out.
referencesFixtures : List String
referencesFixtures = [
  "binder_loc",
  "correctness",
  "dup_field_def",
  "iface_collide",
  "iface_method_loc",
  "iface_ty_collide",
  "impl_method",
  "multiclause",
]

{- | Everything wrong with one `references_fixtures/<name>/` project: a
   `refindex_main --dump` over its `main.mdk`, path-normalized the same way
   the retired script's `sed` was, diffed against `expected.golden`. -}
referencesFixtureFailure : String -> <Exec, FileRead, IO> Option String
referencesFixtureFailure name =
  let dir = underRoot "test/references_fixtures/\{name}"
  let bin = underRoot "test/bin/refindex_main"
  let rt = underRoot "stdlib/runtime.mdk"
  let core = underRoot "stdlib/core.mdk"
  match boundedVerb bin ["--dump", rt, core, "\{dir}/main.mdk", dir]
    Err e => Some "\{name}: could not spawn refindex_main: \{e}"
    Ok (code, out, err) => match processFailure (basename bin) name code err
      Some m => Some m
      None =>
        let got = chompNewlines (replaceAll "\{dir}/" "" out)
        match readFile "\{dir}/expected.golden"
          Err e => Some "\{name}: no readable golden: \{e}"
          Ok raw =>
            let want = chompNewlines raw
            if want == got then None else Some "\{name}: \{diffNote want got}"

-- # `diff_compiler_effect_param`

effectParamFixture : String
effectParamFixture = "test/diff_fixtures/effect_param.mdk"

effectParamSnapshot : String
effectParamSnapshot = "test/snapshots/diff_fixtures_types/effect_param.md"

{- | Stage-2a's parameterized effect surface (`effect Net Prefix`,
   `<Net "a.com/foo">`) accepted by the native CLI, inferred correctly, and
   agreeing with the committed `# TYPES_USER` snapshot. -}
effectParamFailures : <Exec, FileRead, IO> List String
effectParamFailures =
  let fix = underRoot effectParamFixture
  let native = underRoot "medaka"
  let host = underRoot "test/bin/check_main"
  let rt = underRoot "stdlib/runtime.mdk"
  let core = underRoot "stdlib/core.mdk"
  match boundedVerb native ["check", fix]
    Err e => ["native-cli/check: could not spawn: \{e}"]
    Ok (code, natOut, natErr) =>
      match processFailure "medaka" "native-cli/check" code natErr
        Some m => [m]
        None =>
          let natText = natOut ++ natErr
          let acceptFail =
            if hasParseErr natText then
              Some
                "native-cli/check emitted an error accepting effect-param syntax"
            else
              None
          let inferFail =
            if containsAll natText [
              "fetch : String -> <FFI, Net \"a.com/foo\"> String",
              "netGet : String -> <FFI, Net \"a.com/foo\"> String",
            ] then
              None
            else
              Some "native-cli/check did not infer the <Net \"a.com/foo\"> rows"
          let typesFail =
            effectTypesSuperset effectParamSnapshot host rt core fix
          let graded = [acceptFail, inferFail, typesFail]
          countFloor "effect-param assertions" 3 graded ++ somes graded

-- # `diff_compiler_effect_hole`

effectHoleFixture : String
effectHoleFixture = "test/diff_fixtures/effect_param_hole.mdk"

effectHoleSnapshot : String
effectHoleSnapshot = "test/snapshots/diff_fixtures_types/effect_param_hole.md"

effectHoleWs2Src : String
effectHoleWs2Src = unlines [
  "effect Net Prefix",
  "extern netGet : (url : String) -> <FFI, Net url> String",
  "fetch _ =",
  "  let dest = \"a.com/foo\"",
  "  netGet dest",
  "main : <IO> Unit",
  "main = println \"x\"",
]

effectHoleRejectSiblingSrc : String
effectHoleRejectSiblingSrc = unlines [
  "effect Net Prefix",
  "extern netGet : (url : String) -> <FFI, Net url> String",
  "fetch : Unit -> <FFI, Net \"a.com/*\"> String",
  "fetch _ = netGet \"a.com.evil.com/x\"",
  "main : <IO> Unit",
  "main = println \"x\"",
]

effectHoleRejectComputedSrc : String
effectHoleRejectComputedSrc = unlines [
  "effect Net Prefix",
  "extern netGet : (url : String) -> <FFI, Net url> String",
  "fetch : String -> <FFI, Net \"a.com/*\"> String",
  "fetch url = netGet url",
  "main : <IO> Unit",
  "main = println \"x\"",
]

effectHoleRejectOuterComputedSrc : String
effectHoleRejectOuterComputedSrc = unlines [
  "effect Net Prefix",
  "extern netGet : (url : String) -> <FFI, Net url> String",
  "fetch : String -> <FFI, Net \"a.com/*\"> String",
  "fetch url =",
  "  let dest = url",
  "  netGet dest",
  "main : <IO> Unit",
  "main = println \"x\"",
]

{- | Writes `name`.mdk under `scratch` as `src`, then runs `use` on its
   path. `scratch` is shared across every synthesized fixture this test
   needs — `test_process.scratchDir` is a top-level nullary, evaluated ONCE
   per process (`probe_runner.ownScratch`'s own warning), so a helper that
   called `scratchDir` and then `rm -rf`ed it per fixture would delete the
   ONE shared directory out from under every fixture after the first. -}
withScratchFile : String ->
  String ->
  String ->
  (String -> <Exec, FileRead, IO> Option String) ->
  <Exec, FileWrite, IO> Option String
withScratchFile scratch name src use =
  let f = "\{scratch}/\{name}.mdk"
  match writeFile f src
    Err e => Some "\{name}: could not write \{f}: \{e}"
    Ok () => use f

{- | Stage-2b's inferred-hole surface (`<Net>`), the α-derived wildcard
   admission, and the delimiter-aware rejections the WS-2 scope-seeding
   soundness rule depends on (#440-adjacent, WS-2). -}
effectHoleFailures : <Exec, FileWrite, FileRead, IO> List String
effectHoleFailures =
  let fix = underRoot effectHoleFixture
  let native = underRoot "medaka"
  let host = underRoot "test/bin/check_main"
  let rt = underRoot "stdlib/runtime.mdk"
  let core = underRoot "stdlib/core.mdk"
  match boundedVerb native ["check", fix]
    Err e => ["native-cli/check: could not spawn: \{e}"]
    Ok (code, natOut, natErr) =>
      match processFailure "medaka" "native-cli/check" code natErr
        Some m => [m]
        None =>
          let natText = natOut ++ natErr
          let acceptFail =
            if hasParseErr natText then
              Some
                "native-cli/check emitted an error accepting the named-extern fixture"
            else
              None
          let inferFail =
            if containsAll natText [
              "netGet : (url : String) -> <FFI, Net url> String",
              "fetch : Unit -> <FFI, Net \"a.com/*\"> String",
            ] then
              None
            else
              Some "native-cli/check did not infer the hole/wildcard rows"
          let typesFail =
            effectTypesSuperset effectHoleSnapshot host rt core fix
          let synthesized = match scratchDir
            Err e => Err "could not make a scratch directory: \{e}"
            Ok scratch =>
              let ws2Fail =
                withScratchFile
                  scratch
                  "ws2_outer"
                  effectHoleWs2Src
                  (effectHoleWs2Check host rt core)
              let rejectSibling = withScratchFile
                scratch
                "reject_sibling"
                effectHoleRejectSiblingSrc
                (f => effectHoleRejectCheck native "reject_sibling" f)
              let rejectComputed = withScratchFile
                scratch
                "reject_computed"
                effectHoleRejectComputedSrc
                (f => effectHoleRejectCheck native "reject_computed" f)
              let rejectOuterComputed = withScratchFile
                scratch
                "reject_outer_computed"
                effectHoleRejectOuterComputedSrc
                (f => effectHoleRejectCheck native "reject_outer_computed" f)
              let _ = runVerb "rm" ["-rf", scratch]
              let synth =
                [ws2Fail, rejectSibling, rejectComputed, rejectOuterComputed]
              Ok
                (countFloor "effect-hole synthesized assertions" 4 synth
                  ++ somes synth)
          let synthFails = match synthesized
            Err e => [e]
            Ok fs => fs
          let graded = [acceptFail, inferFail, typesFail]
          countFloor "effect-hole native assertions" 3 graded
            ++ somes graded
            ++ synthFails

{- | WS-2 scope-seeding (E3 precision): an OUTER-BODY `let` literal reaches
   an inner `<Net>` call site, so the recovered row must carry the
   literal's prefix rather than staying the bare `<Net>` an empty `lets`
   scope would infer. -}
effectHoleWs2Check : String ->
  String ->
  String ->
  String ->
  <Exec, FileRead, IO> Option String
effectHoleWs2Check host rt core f = match boundedVerb host [rt, core, f]
  Err e => Some "WS-2 outer-let: could not spawn check_main: \{e}"
  Ok (code, out, err) =>
    match processFailure "check_main" "WS-2 outer-let" code err
      Some m => Some m
      None =>
        let text =
          chompNewlines (unlines (sort (lines (stripUnitAutoPrint out))))
        if contains "fetch : a -> <FFI, Net \"a.com/foo\"> String" text then
          None
        else
          Some "WS-2: outer-let row not recovered"

-- | `native check f` must reject: a nonzero exit, or an error/`Effectful`
-- capability diagnostic on its combined output.
effectHoleRejectCheck : String -> String -> String -> <Exec, IO> Option String
effectHoleRejectCheck native name f = match boundedVerb native ["check", f]
  Err e => Some "\{name}: could not spawn native check: \{e}"
  Ok (code, out, err) =>
    let low = toLower (out ++ err)
    if code /= 0 || contains "error" low || contains "effectful" low then
      None
    else
      Some "\{name}: native did not reject (rc=\{intToString code})"

-- # `diff_compiler_typecheck_errors`

typecheckErrorFixturesDir : String
typecheckErrorFixturesDir = "test/typecheck_error_fixtures"

{- | How many fixtures that directory held when this block was written. The
   corpus is scanned rather than listed, and `fixtureFiles`' own floor only
   rules out an EMPTY scan — a corpus that lost fifty fixtures still reports
   nothing. -}
typecheckErrorFixtureCount : Int
typecheckErrorFixtureCount = 134

{- | Fixtures whose documented error depends on the prelude (#11: an integer
   literal desugars to `fromInt`, so the no-prelude driver structurally
   cannot resolve `Num` and would wrongly accept). These run ONLY through
   the prelude-aware driver; every other fixture runs through both. -}
typecheckPreludeDep : List String
typecheckPreludeDep = [
  "effect_ctor_binder_shadow.mdk",
  "effect_socket_ok.mdk",
  "effect_socket_launder.mdk",
  "effect_socket_forge.mdk",
  "effect_socket_redeclare.mdk",
  "effect_socket_redeclare_ok.mdk",
  "effect_data_field_ok.mdk",
  "effect_data_field_launder.mdk",
  "effect_existential_ok.mdk",
  "effect_existential_launder.mdk",
  "effect_phantom_export.mdk",
  "effect_named_authority_scope_launder.mdk",
  "effect_named_authority_scope_ok.mdk",
  "effect_named_authority_method_launder.mdk",
  "effect_named_authority_method_ok.mdk",
  "effect_catalog_position_launder.mdk",
  "effect_catalog_position_ok.mdk",
  "effect_prefix_exact.mdk",
  "effect_named_authority_launder.mdk",
  "effect_named_authority_ok.mdk",
  "effect_named_authority_dynamic_launder.mdk",
  "effect_named_authority_binder_errors.mdk",
  "effect_named_authority_ref_launder.mdk",
  "effect_named_authority_ref_ok.mdk",
  "effect_rename_destination_launder.mdk",
  "effect_rename_destination_ok.mdk",
  "effect_prefix_join_render.mdk",
  "effect_deferred_callback_launder.mdk",
  "effect_deferred_callback_eager_ok.mdk",
  "int_vs_string.mdk",
  "value_restriction.mdk",
  "value_restriction_scc.mdk",
  "value_restriction_sig_pointfree.mdk",
  "value_restriction_sig_expansive.mdk",
  "value_restriction_sig_variable_ok.mdk",
  "missing_super_impl.mdk",
  "cyclic_superinterface.mdk",
  "ambiguous_impl.mdk",
  "ambiguous_return_nested.mdk",
  "ambiguous_return_noconstraint.mdk",
  "do_bind_annot_mismatch.mdk",
  "do_not_thenable.mdk",
  "nested_requires_function_key.mdk",
  "semigroup_no_impl.mdk",
  "negate_no_impl.mdk",
  "nonlinear_head_inconsistent.mdk",
  "effect_impl_launder_cb.mdk",
  "effect_impl_launder_ghost.mdk",
  "effect_impl_launder_mixed.mdk",
  "effect_impl_launder_retlam.mdk",
  "impl_pins_method_tyvar.mdk",
  "impl_pins_method_tyvar_num.mdk",
  "impl_pins_method_tyvar_tuple.mdk",
  "impl_collapses_method_tyvars.mdk",
  "impl_effvar_offspine_launder.mdk",
  "impl_default_pins_method_tyvar.mdk",
  "impl_method_constraint_ok.mdk",
  "impl_constraint_via_helper.mdk",
  "iface_effvar_arg_uncovered.mdk",
  "iface_effvar_arg_only.mdk",
  "default_generic_pins_tyvar.mdk",
  "impl_constraint_via_local_alias.mdk",
  "default_generic_effect_launder.mdk",
  "impl_shadow_generalized_local_ok.mdk",
